  "description": "The memory tool resolve's answer (SB-P5-15, migration 071): one tool for every review queue's action, each that queue's own step with its author lock and audit row. queue is the queue the action belongs to. An item leaves its queue once: unchanged true means nothing was written, because it was no longer waiting, in that word or another, and its message says so and which tool changes it from there. still_counted true says the brief's section for that queue counted it and still does, as after a snooze to within 48 hours or a copy with another flag standing. newly_counted true says it did not and now does, so that section's count rose by one: only a snooze from past the 48 hours into them, which answers still_counted false. Of a memory: a write's fields (no memory's words, a project by id and slug only) and the field changed, with a date's due and before and a decision's result, previous and review_at when the step ran; a second resolve carries the place alone. Of an insight: review and view. Of a candidate: decision, note, insight_id (only to a reader of that insight's scope) and notice, since a note is a client's words. Listed and answered only with memory.tools on (contracts/README.md 2.1). The JSON in its text content, and on success the same as its structured content; a refusal is isError true with the refusal body: needs_person (release, settle_keep_both or settle_replace, a person's alone, answered alike whatever the id names, nothing read), held (a memory held for review), retracted (one marked wrong), unknown (no item the caller reads by that id), forbidden (not this login's: the author lock, or an insight this login saved), conflict (a stale expected_revision), invalid (an argument that does not go with the action, an until that has come, received on what the person owes, a replaced insight).",
